e-claude.webp","alt","Minimal Rogue first-floor gameplay with the player, breakable blocks, corridor, HP and stamina HUD, and block-cracking log.","https://hirotaka-adachi.itch.io/minimal-rogue","width",1280,"height",720,"credit","GameMap browser capture","list","attribution","Creator-attributed clients / models (not inferred from related tools)","items",[80],"Claude Code","links","Related resources",[86],"resourceIds","section",{"_57":80,"_25":87},"/resources/claude-code/","Creator evidence",[91],"evidence",{"_57":92,"_25":68,"_93":94},"Read the author’s Claude Code and SUNO attribution","note","The creator identifies Claude Code for development, SUNO AI for music, links the complete repository and explicitly describes the work as created entirely using AI. No model version or full development transcript is supplied.","Source contents","complete project","Project source",[99],{"_57":100,"_25":101,"_93":102},"Open the complete game project","https://github.com/HirotakaAdachi/Rogue/tree/anonymous-release","Complete static HTML/CSS/JavaScript project and four MP3 tracks; serve the root over HTTP without a package install or build step. MIT code license is included; SUNO music is credited without a separate music license. The reviewed public source index references script version 549, while the itch build references 581, so the two releases are not claimed to be byte-identical.","Access type","playable","demo","Play or run",[108],{"_57":109,"_25":68,"_93":110},"Play Minimal Rogue on itch.io","Browser keyboard game. Enter confirms the opening and tutorial; arrows move, Space defends, and X opens the menu. A short first-floor run verified movement, block-cracking feedback and the command menu. Later floors, saves and a complete run were not tested.","Game platform","itch.io","Guide format","disclosure","tutorial","Build story / tutorial",[118],{"_57":119,"_25":68,"_93":-7},"Read the creator’s AI and source-code notes","Study this workflow","ordered",true,[124,125,126,127],"Run the browser game, choose a new game and language, and confirm the opening and tutorial with Enter.","Use the arrow keys to explore the first room, Space to defend and X to open the command menu.","Read the creator’s AI disclosure and inspect the complete HTML, CSS, JavaScript and music files.","Serve the source folder over HTTP, change one room or stamina rule, and check movement, interactions and a new run.","AI workflow / foundation context","Hirotaka Adachi names Claude Code as the development tool and SUNO AI for music, and describes the work as entirely AI-created. The exact coding model is not identified. The public project contains the game renderer, rules, interface and four music files; the creator’s claim does not establish autonomous development without human direction.","aiUse","guidance","Creation category","AI-generated (creator attribution)","category","provenance","Track","2D","track","metadata","Engine","Canvas 2D · Vanilla JavaScript · HTML/CSS UI","engine","lead","2d","ai-generated",[124,125,126,127],{"_57":119,"_25":68,"_17":114},{"_57":109,"_25":68,"_17":104,"_93":110},{"_57":100,"_25":101,"_153":154,"_93":102},{"_57":92,"_25":68,"_93":94},[152],"claude-code","scope","complete-project",{"_156":157},"documents",{"_158":159,"_160":161},"en",[163,167,168,169,166,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,178,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199,200,201,165,202,164,203,204,205,206,207,208,209,210,211,212,213,214,215,216,217,218,219,220],"zh",[162,163,164,165,166],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production